Computerd for macOS builds on what these MIT-licensed projects worked out. No file is copied from them; where
Computerd uses the same undocumented values, they are named here so a reader can check them against their source.

Cua Driver (https://github.com/trycua/cua, libs/cua-driver), read at 377b0fee21559d770bbb7fe6a772de2a7611a371
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Cua AI, Inc.
  - SkyLight's pid-routed events (SLEventPostToPid) and the window fields 40, 91 and 92 that aim them.
  - CGEventSetWindowLocation reading a window point on macOS 27 and later, a screen point before.
  - Electron's AXManualAccessibility; the messaging timeout of a second or less on every accessibility call.
  - Pressing a menu item by its AXMenuItemCmdChar for a key chord sent to an app in the background.
  - The capture alert's schedule in replayd's ScreenCaptureApprovals.plist (scripts/seed-tcc.sh).

open-computer-use (https://github.com/iFurySt/open-computer-use), read at fccf49abeea10726d58b5acba32b205843cb5f56
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Leo
  - The SkyLight symbols resolved with dlsym and their C signatures (Sources/ComputerdMac/SkyLight.swift).
  - The click recipe: a move, an off-screen primer press, the presses at the point with their click state, gesture
    phase and click group, posted through both SkyLight's path and the public one (Sources/ComputerdMac/Input.swift).
  - The synthetic focus records (activation 0x0D, key window 0x10) that let a background window take keys.

Peekaboo (https://github.com/steipete/Peekaboo), read at 69764083b16397845dc68b5c0ddb4f674290ae70
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Peter Steinberger
  - The shape: one app in the Aqua session holds every grant, and a command started anywhere (an SSH session) relays
    to it, so macOS judges each action by the app's signature.

yabai (https://github.com/koekeishiya/yabai), MIT License
  - The event record layouts above were first recovered there.

